    <string name="settings_breakdown_title">Per-server traffic breakdown</string>
    <string name="settings_breakdown_summary">Show how much traffic went through the proxy versus direct. While connected, this opens a diagnostics port that other apps on your device can also read — leave it off unless you need it.</string>
    <!-- F2 / ruling R39: TunnelService.startCore reads this setting once, at connect, and is
         deliberately not restarted just to apply a change (ARCHITECTURE.md §10.4) — a working
         tunnel is not torn down to close a diagnostics port. These are shown while a session is
         up and the switch has been changed since. The off case is the security-relevant one: it
         must not imply the running session's exposure has already ended. -->
    <string name="settings_breakdown_pending_off">Off for new connections. This session\'s diagnostics port stays open to other apps until you reconnect.</string>
    <string name="settings_breakdown_pending_on">On for new connections. This session won\'t start collecting until you reconnect.</string>
